      "message": "My main use case for hashing spans was to have types used as keys to hash maps, but they are very often a struct that wraps the span. This was a fairly light weight way of using the span hashing behavior without requiring a custom Hash struct and additional template arg to SkTHashMap.\n\nA reasonable alternative would be if we declared a hash wrapper template:\n\n    template\u003cE\u003e\n    struct AsSpan {\n        template \u003ctypename K\u003e\n        uint32_t operator()(const K\u0026 k) const {\n            return SkGoodHash()(SkSpan\u003cE\u003e{k});\n        }\n    };\n    \nThe `span_view` declaration lets the wrapping type control its hash, whereas the `Hash` trait wrapper requires users of the span-wrapper know to adjust their maps.",
